    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Accounting_R160995-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to five (5) documents in the Application Documents section. If necessary, please consider combining documents into one file. If you require any assistance with including the necessary documents in the application process, please reach out to HRConnection@osu.edu . Resume parsing is not effective on documents which exceed one (1) page.  As a result, it is not recommended to select Autofill with Resume when applying if using a resume or CV which exceeds one (1) page. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Assistant Professor of Accounting Department: Fisher College | Accounting and Management Information Systems The Fisher College of Business at The Ohio State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in accounting at the Assistant Professor rank. Candidates will be appointed in the Department of Accounting and Management Information Systems. Candidates are expected to demonstrate the potential for high impact scholarly productivity, high-quality teaching, and high-quality service to the department, the college, and the profession. All courses are taught in person on the University’s main campus in Columbus, Ohio.   Immigration/visa sponsorship may be available in very limited situations (e.g., F1/OPT to H-1b, H-1b change of employer), but all decisions concerning immigration/visa sponsorship will depend on an evaluation of complexity and risk.   Performance Objectives Demonstrate the potential for outstanding achievement in research. Sustain a record of impactful peer-reviewed publications in top-tier business journals. Create and deliver effective course materials. Create an engaging classroom environment. Demonstrate commitment to student success. Effective service to the Department, the College and/or University, and to the greater academic and business community. Collaborate effectively with colleagues in research, teaching, and service.   Education and Experience Requirements Candidates must have completed a Ph.D. in Accounting (or closely related field with a clear accounting focus) on or after January 1, 2025 or expect to complete their Ph.D. in the near future.   Candidates must demonstrate the following: The potential for outstanding achievement in research and teaching in accounting An emerging high-quality research pipeline The potential to collaborate with colleagues through research and service The ability to communicate complex ideas clearly and independently    Ideal candidates will also demonstrate the following: Successful teaching experience at the university level   Additional Information Assistant Professors in this department currently have a base salary of $250,000-$280,000. The offer for this position will be based on internal equity and the candidate's qualifications.    Ohio State provides access to a depth and breadth of opportunities and resources. Starting your first day, Ohio State offers you a comprehensive benefits package . The College: Fisher College of Business has a rich research tradition and engages through the college and the Graduate School in programs at the undergraduate, master and doctoral levels. The nationally ranked Fisher College of Business is one of 15 colleges within the university, with approximately 10,000 undergraduate and 1,200 graduate students.   Department Information: The Department of Accounting & Management Information Systems is home to outstanding faculty, research, programs, and alumni. The department's mission is to advance the disciplines of Accounting and Management Information Systems through excellence in scholarly research and education, and through meaningful outreach activities. The department, which is a major unit within the Fisher College of Business, has a rich research tradition and engages through the college and the Graduate School in programs at the undergraduate, master and doctoral levels.   The University: Ohio State is a top-20 public university, and its Ohio State Wexner Medical Center is one of America’s leading academic health centers. Eligible Ohio State employees receive comprehensive benefits packages, including medical, dental and vision insurance, tuition assistance for employees and their dependents, and state or alternative retirement options with competitive employer contributions.   Grounded in Ohio State University’s Shared Values , our university community welcomes differences, encourages open-minded exploration and courageous thinking, and upholds freedom of expression.   Ohio State is a dynamic community where opportunity thrives, and individuals transform themselves and their world. Positions are available in countless fields and specialties. Become a Buckeye and contribute to an incredible legacy that serves to guide our future and shape a better tomorrow.   The Ohio State University is committed to enhancing academic excellence. Recruiting, supporting, and retaining faculty of the highest caliber is a core component of this commitment. The Office of Academic Affairs (OAA) has established central resources to focus on offering support to new and prospective faculty and their loved ones. Service offerings include dual career partner consultation, potential employer and/or employment opportunity identification, consultation and resources related to relocation, as well as identifying opportunities to engage on campus and in the surrounding community.  While employment opportunities are not guaranteed, resources and consultation are available.  More information about dual career and faculty recruitment can be found here .   In addition to being responsive to dual-career opportunities, we strongly promote work-life balance to support our community members through a suite of institutionalized policies.  Ohio State is a member of the Michigan, Ohio, Western Pennsylvania & West Virginia HERC.   Located in Ohio’s capital city, Ohio State’s Columbus campus is near the center of a rapidly growing and vibrant metropolitan area with a population of over 1.5 million. The area offers a wide range of affordable housing, many cultural and recreational opportunities, excellent schools, and a strong economy based on government as well as service, transportation, and technology industries. Additional information about the Columbus area is available here . Beyond its Columbus campus, Ohio State has four regional campuses including Ohio State Lima, Ohio State Mansfield, Ohio State Marion, and Ohio State Newark, in addition to the College of Food, Agricultural, and Environmental Sciences (CFAES) Wooster Campus, which houses Ohio State ATI.   The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability.     Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check. Additionally, there may be further requirements specific to the college or unit, which could include drug and health screenings, as well as faculty misconduct checks depending on the rank of the position. Additional Information: How to Apply: To be considered, please submit your application electronically via Workday. Application closes midnight, November 18th, 2026.   Required Application Materials: Cover letter Curriculum Vita (CV) Statements of Research and Teaching Primary Research Paper (e.g., Job Market Paper or Dissertation) Secondary Research Paper (working paper or publication) At least two Letters of Recommendation After your application has been processed, you will receive a notification asking you to submit the names of your references, who will receive a link to upload their letter Applicants should instruct letter writers that letters must be received by November 22, 2026 We encourage at least one letter from a dissertation committee member and at least one letter from a research collaborator Location: Fisher Hall (0249) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift The Ohio State University believes in diversity in people and ideas. What Ohio State does matters. And how we do it matters. When we are at our best, we make a real difference to people. Our size, breadth, geography, history and standard of excellence position us to drive the future of higher education. We believe that the university should be a place where people can work and learn together in a safe environment, free of violence, harassment, discrimination, exploitation, or intimidation. As such, finalists for any faculty position that carries tenure must sign an authorization and disclosure form, which will allow current or prior employer(s) to share information to the University regarding any findings of employment-related misconduct or disciplinary proceedings against a candidate and/or any pending investigations related to alleged misconduct. Such information shall include findings and pending investigations with respect to sexual harassment, violence, or harassment; research misconduct; financial fraud or misconduct; foreign influence violations, grant misuse or misconduct; and/or any other type of finding or pending investigation relating to a candidate’s employer’s policies and rules governing faculty conduct that may reasonably be expected to affect a candidate’s appointment. If the University becomes aware of any past finding of misconduct or pending investigations that were not disclosed, Ohio State will treat that as a serious omission and reserves the right to rescind an offer or terminate employment. Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Kokosing-Endowed-Chair-Associate-Full-Professor_R158556": {
      "title": "Kokosing Endowed Chair Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to five (5) documents in the Application Documents section. If necessary, please consider combining documents into one file. If you require any assistance with including the necessary documents in the application process, please reach out to HRConnection@osu.edu . Resume parsing is not effective on documents which exceed one (1) page.  As a result, it is not recommended to select Autofill with Resume when applying if using a resume or CV which exceeds one (1) page. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Kokosing Endowed Chair Associate/Full Professor Department: FAES | Food, Agricultural and Biological Engineering The Department of Food, Agricultural and Biological Engineering (FABE) at The Ohio State University (OSU) invites applications for the Kokosing Endowed Chair in Construction Management. This endowed faculty position offers an exceptional opportunity for an accomplished leader to advance construction management education, workforce development, industry engagement, and, for tenure-track candidates, research. We seek an individual who will strengthen the integration of theory and practice while building partnerships among academia, industry, government agencies, and professional organizations. The successful candidate will provide strategic leadership for Ohio State's nationally recognized Construction Management program and help position it as a national leader in preparing the next generation of construction professionals. This includes engaging at the local and national level with industry. Areas of expertise may include heavy civil infrastructure, construction engineering, commercial building, construction project management, project delivery, digital construction, building information modeling (BIM), virtual design and construction (VDC), construction automation and robotics, artificial intelligence, digital twins, advanced sensing technologies, structural systems design and construction, construction safety, concrete construction, sustainability, site development, and workforce development. Candidates appointed to either the tenure-track or professional practice track will provide leadership in undergraduate education through teaching, curriculum innovation, student mentoring, and program development. Expertise to lead teaching in one or more of the following areas is desirable: construction methods and materials specifically including soils, aggregates, and structural materials, advanced estimating, advanced scheduling and project controls, project management, heavy civil construction, construction equipment and operations, BIM, VDC, and emerging construction technologies. The successful candidate shall provide leadership and coordination across OSU’s construction-related academic programs by fostering collaboration among FABE, the Agricultural Technical Institute (ATI), and the Department of Civil, Environmental and Geodetic Engineering (CEGE). This leadership will coordinate curriculum across campuses, including teaching across campuses as well, which will strengthen transfer pathways, expand interdisciplinary educational opportunities, enhance student recruitment and retention, and deepen engagement with industry partners to address Ohio's growing construction workforce needs.   For candidates appointed to the tenure-track, the Kokosing Endowed Chair is expected to establish and sustain a nationally recognized, externally funded research program that advances the construction industry through innovative scholarship and technology development. Research areas may include digital construction, construction automation and robotics, artificial intelligence, digital twins, advanced sensing, project delivery, infrastructure resilience, construction safety, sustainability, and workforce innovation. The successful candidate will mentor graduate students, secure competitive external funding, and develop interdisciplinary research and outreach programs that leverage OSU’s exceptional faculty expertise, research centers, statewide facilities, and industry partnerships. Active collaboration with contractors, infrastructure owners, transportation agencies, professional societies, industry associations, technology providers, and government organizations will be essential to translating research into practice and enhancing the national prominence of OSU’s Construction Management program . Performance Objectives Responsibilities for Both Tenure-Track and Professional Practice Appointments: Teach approximately three to five courses annually (depending on appointment), primarily within the Construction Management program, while contributing to undergraduate curriculum development, innovation, and continuous improvement. Demonstrate excellence in teaching and mentoring by fostering an inclusive learning environment that prepares students with the technical, professional, and leadership skills needed for successful careers in construction management and related fields. Provide leadership in coordinating and strengthening construction-related academic programs across FABE, ATI, and CEGE. Responsibilities include enhancing student pathways, supporting interdisciplinary programming, advancing workforce development initiatives, and promoting collaboration among academic units. Advise and mentor undergraduate students, including Construction Management majors, honors students, student competition teams, and student organizations, while supporting recruitment, retention, career development, and experiential learning opportunities. Develop and sustain collaborative partnerships with construction contractors, infrastructure owners, government agencies, professional societies, industry associations, labor organizations, technology providers, alumni, and other industry stakeholders to strengthen teaching, outreach, workforce development, and industry engagement. Work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, industry partners, and external stakeholders to advance OSU’s land-grant mission through excellence in teaching, outreach, service, and industry engagement. Provide leadership and service to the department, college, university, profession, and construction industry through committee assignments, accreditation activities, professional organizations, workforce development initiatives, advisory boards, and other responsibilities appropriate for an endowed chair. Disseminate scholarly contributions through high-impact peer-reviewed publications, presentations at national and international conferences, and engagement with industry and professional organizations. Responsibilities for Tenure-Track Appointments Establish and sustain a nationally recognized, externally funded research and scholarship program in construction management, construction engineering, heavy civil infrastructure, digital construction, project delivery, construction technologies, or related fields. Advise and mentor graduate students, including master's and doctoral candidates, while fostering interdisciplinary research and supporting the professional development of future scholars. Secure and manage competitive external funding from federal and state agencies, foundations, and industry partners to support research, graduate education, workforce development, and technology transfer. Develop collaborative, multidisciplinary research programs that leverage OSU’s faculty expertise, research centers, statewide facilities, and industry partnerships to address emerging challenges facing the construction industry. Education and Experience Requirements Required for Professional Practice and Tenure-Track Faculty: Earned Ph.D. in Construction Management, Civil Engineering, Construction Engineering, Architectural Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated excellence in teaching and curriculum development in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or closely related disciplines. Demonstrated experience or engagement in developing collaborative relationships with local and national industry partners, government agencies, and professional organizations. Evidence of leadership in heavy civil construction or construction management, advancing construction education, research, workforce development, or industry engagement. Excellent verbal and written communication skills and a demonstrated ability to engage effectively with diverse academic, industry, and stakeholder audiences. Demonstrated commitment to teaching, recruiting, mentoring, and advising a diverse student population. Eligibility to work effectively in a collaborative, interdisciplinary environment involving faculty, students, industry leaders, and external partners.   Required for Tenure-Track Faculty: Record of scholarly achievement and national recognition commensurate with appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor with tenure. Demonstrated expertise conducting applied and/or fundamental research in one or more areas relevant to the construction industry, including but not limited to construction engineering, project management, heavy civil infrastructure, construction technologies, digital construction, building information modeling (BIM), virtual design and construction (VDC), construction automation, robotics, artificial intelligence, digital twins, infrastructure systems, sustainability, or construction safety. Demonstrated success in securing and managing externally funded research, industry-sponsored projects, or other competitive funding programs. Preferred for Tenure-Track and Professional Practice Faculty: Professional experience in the construction industry, engineering consulting, construction operations, project delivery, or related professional practice. Professional Engineer (P.E.), Certified Professional Constructor (CPC), Design-Build Professional (DBIA), Project Management Professional (PMP), or other relevant professional credentials. Demonstrated leadership in construction industry trade associations, professional societies, standards organizations, or workforce development initiatives. Experience developing and managing industry-academic partnerships, research centers, workforce training programs, or large multidisciplinary initiatives. Expertise in emerging areas of construction innovation, including digital construction, artificial intelligence, automation, robotics, autonomous equipment, advanced sensing, data analytics, digital twins, or smart infrastructure systems. Demonstrated ability to enhance student career readiness through experiential learning, internships, industry engagement, and professional mentoring. Additional Information: How to Apply To be considered, please submit your application electronically via Workday. Application materials must include the following: Cover letter describing your qualifications, areas of expertise, career goals, and alignment with desired qualifications and preferred qualifications where applicable Curriculum Vita (CV) Statement of Teaching and Mentoring 1-2 pages describing your teaching philosophy, mentoring approach, instructional experience, curriculum development, commitment to student success, and vision for advancing undergraduate and graduate education, experiential learning, workforce development, and the Construction Management program at OSU. Statement of Industry Engagement 1 page describing your experience and vision for engaging with industry, government agencies, professional societies, and other stakeholders to advance teaching, workforce development, applied research and technology transfer (as appropriate), continuing education, and collaborative partnerships that strengthen the Construction Management program and serve the construction industry. Statement of Research: 1-page describing your research accomplishments, current areas of scholarship, and future research vision. The statement should highlight the significance and impact of your work, plans for developing or expanding an externally funded research program, opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration, mentoring of graduate students, and strategies for translating research into practice through partnerships with industry, government agencies, and professional organizations. Professional practice candidates are not required to submit a research statement. Initial consideration will be given to applications received by December 6, 2026 . Review of applications will continue until the position has been filled. We welcome informal inquiries, which can be made by contacting Search Committee Chair Dr. John Fulton at fulton.20@osu.edu. Department/School Information FABE is a multidisciplinary tenure-initiating unit (TIU) within The Ohio State University's College of Food, Agricultural, and Environmental Sciences (CFAES), with the Food, Agricultural and Biological Engineering degree program jointly administered with the College of Engineering. FABE includes approximately 26 faculty, 17 full and part-time lecturers more than 50 staff and research personnel, and nearly 500 undergraduate and graduate students enrolled in four academic programs: Food, Agricultural and Biological Engineering, Agricultural Systems Management, Construction Management, and graduate programs leading to the M.S. and Ph.D. degrees. The department's faculty conduct nationally and internationally recognized research spanning construction and infrastructure systems, precision and digital agriculture, automation and robotics, artificial intelligence, machine systems, controlled environment agriculture, food and bioprocess engineering, water quality and environmental systems, and sustainable agricultural technologies. Through its campuses in Columbus and Wooster, Ohio State University Extension, and a statewide network of research farms and facilities, FABE integrates teaching, research, and outreach to address emerging challenges in agriculture, construction, food systems, and the environment. FABE maintains strong partnerships with industry, government agencies, commodity organizations, and professional societies that provide exceptional opportunities for experiential learning, applied research, workforce development, and technology transfer. The department's graduate program in Food, Agricultural and Biological Engineering is consistently ranked among the nation's top programs by U.S. News & World Report, ranking 10th nationally in the 2026 Best Graduate Engineering Schools rankings. The Construction Management program is accredited by the American Council for Construction Education (ACCE) and is supported by an active Industry Advisory Council that helps guide curriculum, facilities, and strategic priorities. Consistent with Ohio State's land-grant mission and the university's strategic plan, FABE is committed to excellence in teaching, research, outreach, and service while preparing graduates to become leaders in engineering, construction, agriculture, and related industries. Additional information about the department, its academic programs, research, and faculty is available at https://fabe.osu.edu. The College The College of Food, Agricultural, and Environmental Sciences (CFAES) anchors its mission in a simple, yet powerful phrase: We Sustain Life. Faculty, staff and students alike contribute to this mission in a variety of ways. Our outlines the colleges values. These values, which align with the university’s Shared Values, shape our goals of our Strategic Alignment. We are committed to scholarship across three mission areas (teaching, research, Extension) with a commitment to serving our state in addition to the country and world. As a land grant, we are part of a cooperative structure that includes key partners all dedicated to integrating research, education, and Extension to improve the food and agricultural sectors, the environment, and the quality of people’s lives. We educate not just undergraduate and graduate students but learners across the lifespan. We work to ensure groundbreaking scientific discoveries are brought out of the laboratory and into the hands of those who can put them to work. CFAES houses 11 departments/schools with over 20 undergraduate majors and 9 graduate programs , including 3 interdisciplinary programs affiliated with multiple Ohio State colleges. We also administer OSU Extension , which provides robust and relevant programming to Ohioans and beyond in the areas of Agriculture and Natural Resources , 4-H Youth Development , Family and Consumer Sciences , and Community Development . We are one college spanning three campuses: Columbus, CFAES Wooster, and Statewide. Our CFAES Wooster campus includes a large research station and Ohio State’s only two-year academic unit, Ohio State ATI . The Statewide campus includes 11 research stations and Extension offices in all of Ohio’s 88 counties. Our At a Glance provides additional information regarding our size, capacity, and impact as a college. The University Ohio State is a top-20 public university, and its Ohio State Wexner Medical Center is one of America’s leading academic health centers. Eligible Ohio State employees receive comprehensive benefits packages, including medical, dental and vision insurance, tuition assistance for employees and their dependents, and state or alternative retirement options with competitive employer contributions. Grounded in Ohio State University’s Shared Values , our university community welcomes differences, encourages open-minded exploration and courageous thinking, and upholds freedom of expression. Ohio State is a dynamic community where opportunity thrives, and individuals transform themselves and their world. Positions are available in countless fields and specialties. Become a Buckeye and contribute to an incredible legacy that serves to guide our future and shape a better tomorrow. The Ohio State University is committed to enhancing academic excellence. Recruiting, supporting, and retaining faculty of the highest caliber is a core component of this commitment. The Office of Academic Affairs (OAA) has established central resources to focus on offering support to new and prospective faculty and their loved ones. Service offerings include dual career partner consultation, potential employer and/or employment opportunity identification, consultation and resources related to relocation, as well as identifying opportunities to engage on campus and in the surrounding community. While employment opportunities are not guaranteed, resources and consultation are available. More information about dual career and faculty recruitment can be found here. In addition to being responsive to dual-career opportunities, we strongly promote work-life balance to support our community members through a suite of institutionalized policies. Ohio State is a member of the Michigan, Ohio, Western Pennsylvania & West Virginia HERC. Located in Ohio’s capital city, Ohio State’s Columbus campus is near the cen"
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Lecturer_R160906-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to five (5) documents in the Application Documents section. If necessary, please consider combining documents into one file. If you require any assistance with including the necessary documents in the application process, please reach out to HRConnection@osu.edu . Resume parsing is not effective on documents which exceed one (1) page.  As a result, it is not recommended to select Autofill with Resume when applying if using a resume or CV which exceeds one (1) page. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Lecturer Department: Arts and Sciences | Speech Hearing Science Position Overview The Department of Speech and Hearing Science seeks a Lecturer to teach one 3 credit hour course, SHS 4520, Introduction to Clinical Methods in Speech-Language Pathology, during Spring 2027 semester.  In addition to teaching, the Lecturer prepares syllabi and course materials for assigned courses, holds office hours, grades assignments and submits grades by deadlines, and communicates regularly with students.  Performance Objectives Planning and organizing instruction in ways which maximize student learning Meeting scheduled classes and office hours in accordance with university policy Ensuring curriculum implementation and course preparation in accordance with department standards Preparing homework and exams, evaluating, and returning student work in a timely manner to promote learning Maintaining accurate records of students’ progress and submitting final grade roster in accordance with established university deadlines Maintaining confidentiality of student information in accordance with FERPA Education and Experience Requirements Required: Master’s degree in a field appropriate to the subject matter being taught. Desired: Evidence of ability to provide high-quality instruction. Additional Information Ohio State provides access to a depth and breadth of opportunities and resources. Starting your first day, Ohio State offers you a comprehensive benefits package .   How to Apply To be considered, please submit your application electronically via Workday. Application materials must include: Cover letter Curriculum Vita (CV)   Additional Information: The College With more than 80 majors and 100 minors, the College of Arts and Sciences is the academic heart of the university. The Arts and Sciences provides extraordinary opportunities to collaborate across disciplines, blending creativity and analysis to truly be at the forefront of thought. The breadth and depth of knowledge in the college gives students and researchers the critical thinking and adaptability essential for a lifetime of success.  Department Information The Department of Speech and Hearing Science ( https://sphs.osu.edu/ ) is positioned within the College of Arts and Sciences and the Division of the Social and Behavioral Sciences. It consists of 22 full-time faculty across the tenure, clinical, teaching, and research tracks. The Department has four main academic programs: the BA in Speech and Hearing Science, MA in Speech-Language Pathology, AuD in Audiology, and the PhD. The MA and AuD programs are ranked 14th and 9th by U.S. News and World Report. We seek colleagues who will help advance our mission through research and education. The University Ohio State is a top-20 public university, and its Ohio State Wexner Medical Center is one of America’s leading academic health centers. Eligible Ohio State employees receive comprehensive benefits packages, including medical, dental and vision insurance, tuition assistance for employees and their dependents, and state or alternative retirement options with competitive employer contributions.   Grounded in Ohio State University’s  Shared Values , our university community welcomes differences, encourages open-minded exploration and courageous thinking, and upholds freedom of expression. Ohio State promotes a culture of work-life balance through institutionalized policies, programs, and resources that help faculty, staff, and their families thrive both professionally and personally.   Ohio State is a dynamic community where opportunity thrives, and individuals transform themselves and their world. Positions are available in countless fields and specialties. Become a Buckeye and contribute to an incredible legacy that serves to guide our future and shape a better tomorrow.   Located in Ohio’s capital city, Ohio State’s Columbus campus is near the center of a rapidly growing and vibrant metropolitan area with a population of over 1.5 million. The area offers a wide range of affordable housing, many cultural and recreational opportunities, excellent schools, and a strong economy based on government as well as service, transportation, and technology industries. Additional information about the Columbus area is available here . Beyond its Columbus campus, Ohio State has four regional campuses including Ohio State Lima, Ohio State Mansfield, Ohio State Marion, and Ohio State Newark, in addition to the College of Food, Agricultural, and Environmental Sciences (CFAES) Wooster Campus, which houses Ohio State ATI. The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability.     Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check. Additionally, there may be further requirements specific to the college or unit, which could include drug and health screenings, as well as faculty misconduct checks depending on the rank of the position. Location: Pressey Hall (0309) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 10 Shift: First Shift The Ohio State University believes in diversity in people and ideas. What Ohio State does matters. And how we do it matters. When we are at our best, we make a real difference to people. Our size, breadth, geography, history and standard of excellence position us to drive the future of higher education. We believe that the university should be a place where people can work and learn together in a safe environment, free of violence, harassment, discrimination, exploitation, or intimidation. As such, finalists for any faculty position that carries tenure must sign an authorization and disclosure form, which will allow current or prior employer(s) to share information to the University regarding any findings of employment-related misconduct or disciplinary proceedings against a candidate and/or any pending investigations related to alleged misconduct. Such information shall include findings and pending investigations with respect to sexual harassment, violence, or harassment; research misconduct; financial fraud or misconduct; foreign influence violations, grant misuse or misconduct; and/or any other type of finding or pending investigation relating to a candidate’s employer’s policies and rules governing faculty conduct that may reasonably be expected to affect a candidate’s appointment. If the University becomes aware of any past finding of misconduct or pending investigations that were not disclosed, Ohio State will treat that as a serious omission and reserves the right to rescind an offer or terminate employment. Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/College-of-MedicineOffice-of-Health-Sciences/Post-Doctoral-Scholar_R147042-1": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Scholar",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Post Doctoral Scholar Department: Medicine | Neurology Job Description We are inviting applications for 2 postdoctoral positions in our laboratory at The Ohio State University, Wexner Medical Center, Department of Neurology & Neuroscience Research Institute. Our lab focusses on axon-glia interactions and on how glial metabolism regulates axon integrity and myelination (e.g., Nature Neuroscience, PMID 32807950; Nature Neuroscience, PMID 25195104; PNAS, PMID 28484008). Examples for current projects are in vivo and in vitro mechanistic studies on how metabolic perturbations in oligodendrocytes result in compromised axon integrity, and research on metabolic adaptations in Schwann cells/oligodendrocytes that support the survival of injured axons. The Post Doctoral Researcher will pursue specialized research training, education and experience under the guidance of a scientific mentor in the Department of Neurology; plan, design and execute experiments of considerable scope and complexity in the assigned research lab; collect and analyzes data for research sponsored by appropriate agencies and Institutions; identify and select problems to be studied; develop and troubleshoot new experimental techniques and protocols; attend research seminars; contribute to manuscript preparation and support technical writing; participate in preparation of grant applications for extramural funding; perform additional duties as assigned. The necessary requirement is a true passion for science and discovery. The ideal candidate should also have at least 1 first-authored publication in press, and have experience working with murine models in a laboratory setting. Minimum education requirement Doctoral degree in Biological Sciences required Minimum preferred experience The successful candidate should have less than 3 years of prior post-doctoral experience, be highly motivated, and show good communication skills. Strong language and writing skills are important. Requires successful completion of a background check. Selected candidate may be requested to complete a pre-employment physical including a drug screen. Additional Information: Location: Biomedical Research Tower (0112) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Associate-Professor-or-Professor--Director-of-the-Arts-and-Humanities-Artificial-Intelligence-Institute_R159362-1": {
      "title": "Associate Professor or Professor, Director of the Arts and Humanities Artificial Intelligence Institute",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to five (5) documents in the Application Documents section. If necessary, please consider combining documents into one file. If you require any assistance with including the necessary documents in the application process, please reach out to HRConnection@osu.edu . Resume parsing is not effective on documents which exceed one (1) page.  As a result, it is not recommended to select Autofill with Resume when applying if using a resume or CV which exceeds one (1) page. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Associate Professor or Professor, Director of the Arts and Humanities Artificial Intelligence Institute Department: Arts and Sciences | Office of the Deans James Mitchell Endowed Chair and Arts & Humanities Artificial Intelligence Institute Center Director         Rank: Advanced Associate Professor or Professor College of Arts and Sciences Position Overview The Ohio State University seeks the James Mitchell Endowed Chair who will be a center director to provide ambitious and innovative leadership for its newly established Arts and Humanities Artificial Intelligence Institute (AHAII). The aim is to make Ohio State a national hub in the conversation about what it means to be human in the age of AI. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. The director will serve as the administrative head of an emerging and thriving institute, with oversight of facilities, budget, and strategic direction. In addition to their role as the institute leader and administrator, the director will also be a dedicated teacher and distinguished scholar, with a record of accomplishment to merit a tenure-track appointment in an Arts or Humanities department as an advanced Associate Professor or Professor. The new director is expected to foster a collegial and interdisciplinary culture among a community of faculty, staff, and students from varied disciplinary backgrounds. They will be an advocate for the institute and its affiliated faculty and students, providing support and mentorship for scholarly activity while amplifying the voice of the arts and humanities in conversations around AI. Applying their knowledge in developing approaches, manifestations, and discourse tied to matters of AI, the director will guide institute affiliates, outreach endeavors, and student education. The director will have the opportunity to shape renovation plans for AHAII in Hughes Hall, a historic building on the oval and future home of our English Department. The director should be poised to engage with students, faculty, staff, and alumni to build collaborations with arts and humanities departments and interdisciplinary initiatives across the College of Arts and Sciences and the broader university community, Ohio State’s five regional campuses, and community organizations in Ohio and beyond. The successful candidate will be a dedicated educator and a recognized scholar and/or practitioner with expertise in one or more scholarly areas involving artificial intelligence and arts or humanities and will have a 50% FTE (Full Time Equivalent) faculty appointment in an appointment in one of the 21 Arts and Humanities departments in the College of Arts and Sciences with the other 50% FTE appointment as AHAII director. Performance Objectives To provide steady yet innovative leadership to AHAII. To support fundraising efforts in partnership with OSU Advancement. Initiating and partnering on writing grants and exploring industry connections to support AHAII. To manage budgets, resources, and space for the institute. To coordinate arts, humanities, and artificial intelligence initiatives in teaching, scholarship, and engagement in and beyond the college. To help faculty, students, and staff thrive in their roles through leadership, mentoring, and professional development. To advocate for the institute to units around the university, community, and broader academic field. To lead engagement efforts with communities and public/private organizations in and beyond Central Ohio. Education and Experience Requirements Required : Applicants are expected to have an appropriate terminal degree in an area of specialty sufficient to warrant appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor with tenure. National/international record of scholarly or artistic achievement in AI, arts and/or humanities commensurate with the position of advanced Associate Professor or Professor at the Ohio State University, including a distinguished record of creative or scholarly achievement, teaching excellence at the post-secondary level, and professional service; and evidence of continued excellence in creative and/or scholarly achievement. Equivalent outstanding achievement in industry will also be considered. Demonstrated and effective leadership and administrative experience in academia. Demonstrated ability to cultivate positive work relationships with students, colleagues, and staff. Experience in leading and the ability to work successfully across disciplines within a diverse and complex organization. Experience with interdisciplinary collaborations, for example those with other academic units, community partners, and professional academic/arts and humanities organizations. Desired : Experience in fundraising, budgeting, and management. Experience managing an academic program, department, or center. Additional Information Ohio State provides access to a depth and breadth of opportunities and resources. Starting your first day, Ohio State offers you a comprehensive benefits package . How to Apply To be considered, please submit your application electronically via Workday https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Associate-Professor-or-Professor--Director-of-the-Arts-and-Humanities-Artificial-Intelligence-Institute_R159362-1 . Application deadline closes on November 1, 2026. Application materials consist of the following required elements: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and separate research statement. Inquiries may be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Professor Chris Coleman (coleman.1299@osu.edu). You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to THREE documents in the Application Documents section. Please include the following: Attachment 1: Cover Letter: 3-4 page letter, which should include a summary of your leadership experience, overview of your teaching and research and/or creative scholarship, and your philosophy on AI with regards to the Arts and Humanities Attachment 2: CV (Curriculum Vitae): Detailed overview of your scholarly experience, leadership experience, teaching and mentoring experience, service, funding, and publications. Attachment 3: Research Statement: Summary of your past research/creative accomplishments, current work, and proposal for your future research plan as a faculty member. You may be asked for names and contact information for three reference letters at a later date. Additional Information: The College With more than 80 majors and 100 minors, the College of Arts and Sciences is the academic heart of the university. The Arts and Sciences provides extraordinary opportunities to collaborate across disciplines, blending creativity and analysis to truly be at the forefront of thought. The breadth and depth of knowledge in the college gives students and researchers the critical thinking and adaptability essential for a lifetime of success. Center Information AHAII was created in 2025 to coordinate, accelerate, and extend the reach of research, creative work, and public engagement centered on artificial intelligence. This focused hub serves as a vital advocate for the centrality of humanity in every conversation about the shape and use of AI. It builds on more than three-years of activity from more than two dozen interdisciplinary faculty working groups that have explored innovative uses of AI in arts and humanities research; the changing meanings of authorship and creativity; and the ethical, ecological, and social consequences of AI technologies. That work has, among other things, resulted in three new credentials that can be pursued alongside any undergraduate major: certificates in “AI and the Arts” (forthcoming); in “AI, Language, and Mind”; and in “AI, Ethics, and Society.” AHAII will be housed in Hughes Hall as soon as it reopens. Hughes, dedicated in 1949, is the former home to the School of Music and the final significant project in our Arts District. When renovated, it will have a new glass annex facing the Oval, and be home to the Department of English as well as AHAII, linking together our arts and humanities departments. The University Ohio State is a top-20 public university, and its Ohio State Wexner Medical Center is one of America’s leading academic health centers. Eligible Ohio State employees receive comprehensive benefits packages, including medical, dental and vision insurance, tuition assistance for employees and their dependents, and state or alternative retirement options with competitive employer contributions. Located in Ohio’s capital city, Ohio State’s Columbus campus is near the center of a rapidly growing and vibrant metropolitan area with a population of over 1.5 million. The area offers a wide range of affordable housing, many cultural and recreational opportunities, excellent schools, and a strong economy based on government as well as service, transportation, and technology industries. Additional information about the Columbus area is available here . Beyond its Columbus campus, Ohio State has four regional campuses including Ohio State Lima, Ohio State Mansfield, Ohio State Marion, and Ohio State Newark, in addition to the College of Food, Agricultural, and Environmental Sciences (CFAES) Wooster Campus, which houses Ohio State ATI. The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability.    Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check. Additionally, there may be further requirements specific to the college or unit, which could include drug and health screenings, as well as faculty misconduct checks depending on the rank of the position Location: University Hall (0339) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift The Ohio State University believes in diversity in people and ideas. What Ohio State does matters. And how we do it matters. When we are at our best, we make a real difference to people. Our size, breadth, geography, history and standard of excellence position us to drive the future of higher education. We believe that the university should be a place where people can work and learn together in a safe environment, free of violence, harassment, discrimination, exploitation, or intimidation. As such, finalists for any faculty position that carries tenure must sign an authorization and disclosure form, which will allow current or prior employer(s) to share information to the University regarding any findings of employment-related misconduct or disciplinary proceedings against a candidate and/or any pending investigations related to alleged misconduct. Such information shall include findings and pending investigations with respect to sexual harassment, violence, or harassment; research misconduct; financial fraud or misconduct; foreign influence violations, grant misuse or misconduct; and/or any other type of finding or pending investigation relating to a candidate’s employer’s policies and rules governing faculty conduct that may reasonably be expected to affect a candidate’s appointment. If the University becomes aware of any past finding of misconduct or pending investigations that were not disclosed, Ohio State will treat that as a serious omission and reserves the right to rescind an offer or terminate employment. Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Lecturer-in-Finance_R161049-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to five (5) documents in the Application Documents section. If necessary, please consider combining documents into one file. If you require any assistance with including the necessary documents in the application process, please reach out to HRConnection@osu.edu . Resume parsing is not effective on documents which exceed one (1) page.  As a result, it is not recommended to select Autofill with Resume when applying if using a resume or CV which exceeds one (1) page. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Lecturer in Finance Department: Fisher College | Finance The Department of Finance at The Ohio State University’s Max M. Fisher College of Business invites application for a full-time Lecturer. We seek candidates with expertise in all areas of corporate finance and teaching with Excel applications; behavioral finance; investments; and asset management. A strong preference will be given to candidates with the ability to teach a broad spectrum of corporate finance courses across both undergraduate and graduate levels. The appointment is expected to begin in Autumn 2027.   The main tasks will include: teaching in different modalities (in-class, online, hybrid) throughout the academic year, curriculum/syllabus design, content and materials development, and service activities. The selected candidate(s) will be expected to complete activities and support for developing and teaching undergraduate and/or graduate students, depending on chosen candidate’s degree certification.   All in-class courses are taught in person on the University’s main campus in Columbus, Ohio.   Immigration/visa sponsorship may be available in very limited situations (e.g., F1/OPT to H-1b, H-1b change of employer), but all decisions concerning immigration/visa sponsorship will depend on an evaluation of complexity and risk.   Performance Objectives: Demonstrate the potential for outstanding achievement in research. Sustain a record of impactful peer-reviewed publications in top-tier business journals. Create and deliver effective course materials. Create an engaging classroom environment. Demonstrate commitment to student success. Collaborate effectively with fellow instructors. Effective service to the Department, the College and/or University, and to the greater academic and business community.   Education and Experience Requirements: Master’s degree in finance or a related field of study Demonstrated teaching experience Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to effectively engage with students in both traditional and online learning environments. Ability to collaborate with fellow instructors, graduate teaching associates, and undergraduate teaching assistants.   Desired Qualifications: Business experience in finance Experience teaching finance courses at undergraduate and graduate levels     Additional Information:   Lecturers starting in this department currently have a base salary of $120,000. The offer for this position will be based on internal equity and the candidate's qualifications.    Ohio State provides access to a depth and breadth of opportunities and resources. Starting your first day, Ohio State offers you a comprehensive benefits package . The College: Fisher College of Business has a rich research tradition and engages through the college and the Graduate School in programs at the undergraduate, master and doctoral levels. The nationally ranked Fisher College of Business is one of 15 colleges within the university, with approximately 9,000 undergraduate and 1,200 graduate students.   Department Information:  The Department of Finance houses faculty specializing in financial economics, business law, and insurance. Our over 20 faculty members are internationally known researchers and teachers. We provide a vibrant research and teaching atmosphere, characterized by extensive collaboration with a shared goal of conducting leading-edge research and providing students with the skills they need to succeed in the field of finance.   The University: Ohio State is a top-20 public university, and its Ohio State Wexner Medical Center is one of America’s leading academic health centers. Eligible Ohio State employees receive comprehensive benefits packages, including medical, dental and vision insurance, tuition assistance for employees and their dependents, and state or alternative retirement options with competitive employer contributions.   Grounded in Ohio State University’s Shared Values , our university community welcomes differences, encourages open-minded exploration and courageous thinking, and upholds freedom of expression.   Ohio State is a dynamic community where opportunity thrives, and individuals transform themselves and their world. Positions are available in countless fields and specialties. Become a Buckeye and contribute to an incredible legacy that serves to guide our future and shape a better tomorrow.   The Ohio State University is committed to enhancing academic excellence. Recruiting, supporting, and retaining faculty of the highest caliber is a core component of this commitment. The Office of Academic Affairs (OAA) has established central resources to focus on offering support to new and prospective faculty and their loved ones. Service offerings include dual career partner consultation, potential employer and/or employment opportunity identification, consultation and resources related to relocation, as well as identifying opportunities to engage on campus and in the surrounding community.  While employment opportunities are not guaranteed, resources and consultation are available.  More information about dual career and faculty recruitment can be found here .   In addition to being responsive to dual-career opportunities, we strongly promote work-life balance to support our community members through a suite of institutionalized policies.  Ohio State is a member of the Michigan, Ohio, Western Pennsylvania & West Virginia HERC.   Located in Ohio’s capital city, Ohio State’s Columbus campus is near the center of a rapidly growing and vibrant metropolitan area with a population of over 1.5 million. The area offers a wide range of affordable housing, many cultural and recreational opportunities, excellent schools, and a strong economy based on government as well as service, transportation, and technology industries. Additional information about the Columbus area is available here . Beyond its Columbus campus, Ohio State has four regional campuses including Ohio State Lima, Ohio State Mansfield, Ohio State Marion, and Ohio State Newark, in addition to the College of Food, Agricultural, and Environmental Sciences (CFAES) Wooster Campus, which houses Ohio State ATI.   The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability.     Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check. Additionally, there may be further requirements specific to the college or unit, which could include drug and health screenings, as well as faculty misconduct checks depending on the rank of the position. Additional Information: How to Apply:  To be considered, please submit your application electronically via Workday. Application closes 12/31/2026.   Required Application Materials: Cover letter Curriculum Vita (CV) Location: Fisher Hall (0249) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift The Ohio State University believes in diversity in people and ideas. What Ohio State does matters. And how we do it matters. When we are at our best, we make a real difference to people. Our size, breadth, geography, history and standard of excellence position us to drive the future of higher education. We believe that the university should be a place where people can work and learn together in a safe environment, free of violence, harassment, discrimination, exploitation, or intimidation. As such, finalists for any faculty position that carries tenure must sign an authorization and disclosure form, which will allow current or prior employer(s) to share information to the University regarding any findings of employment-related misconduct or disciplinary proceedings against a candidate and/or any pending investigations related to alleged misconduct. Such information shall include findings and pending investigations with respect to sexual harassment, violence, or harassment; research misconduct; financial fraud or misconduct; foreign influence violations, grant misuse or misconduct; and/or any other type of finding or pending investigation relating to a candidate’s employer’s policies and rules governing faculty conduct that may reasonably be expected to affect a candidate’s appointment. If the University becomes aware of any past finding of misconduct or pending investigations that were not disclosed, Ohio State will treat that as a serious omission and reserves the right to rescind an offer or terminate employment. Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
