    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Post-Doctoral-Researcher-Medical-Oncology_R160541-1": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher-Medical Oncology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Post Doctoral Researcher-Medical Oncology Department: Medicine | IM Medical Oncology Come and be a Buckeye! We are hiring! About The [Ansa-Addo Lab] at the OSU Comprehensive Cancer Center There is a Postdoctoral Scholar position opening mentored by Dr. Ephraim Ansa-Addo at The Ohio State University. The over-arching focus of the laboratory is characterizing the roles of various T cell subsets, specifically, regulatory T cells and T follicular helper cells that are present in the tumor microenvironment and their impact on cancer progression. Our lab is highly collaborative, and the selected candidate will work interactively with a multidisciplinary team of physician scientists, cancer biologists, immunologists and biomedical informaticians within the PIIO and OSUCCC. Detailed Position Description: A postdoctoral scholar position in cancer immunology and immunotherapy is available at the Pelotonia Institute for Immuno-Oncology (PIIO), the Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center (OSUCCC). The individual will work on basic and translational tumor immunology with a focus on T cell biology, immune checkpoint blockade and adoptive immunotherapy of cancer – the goal being to develop new treatments for patients. Our over-arching research focuses on various aspects of anti-tumor immunity mediated by antigen-specific T cells. Particularly, we are interested in the biology of T follicular helper (TFH) cells, as well as regulatory T (Treg) cells. This is an exciting opportunity for a highly dedicated, ambitious and creative scientist who can work independently, and as part of a team to join the recently established Immunity and Cancer Laboratory (ICL) in the PIIO. Research in the ICL primarily focuses on characterizing the roles of Treg cells and TFH cells present in the tumor microenvironment (TME), and their impact on cancer progression, as well as the fate-commitment of antitumor T cells to exhaustion. In this regard, we seek to understand how cellular and molecular regulators including the RNA-binding protein, Poly(C)-binding protein (PCBP1) and chromatin-modifying proteins determine the fate and functions of Treg cells in the TME. Interested candidates with demonstrated experience and a strong interest in studying T cell immunology and cancer immunotherapy, as well as some knowledge of bioinformatics are encouraged to apply. Candidates should expect to work interactively with a multidisciplinary team of physician scientists, cancer biologists, immunologists and biomedical informaticians within the PIIO and OSUCCC. Successful applicants will be on the frontline of discovery using a novel single cell platform, systems immunology as well as traditional cellular and molecular immunology and in vivo studies. The PIIO has a unique Industry-Academic relationship, meaning scientists have access to cutting-edge research core facilities and analytical tools including, Multispectral Flow Cytometry, Time-of-Flight Mass Cytometry, GMP Facility for Cell Therapy, Antibody Engineering Facility, Single-Cell RNA Sequencing and Proteomics that comprise a state-of-the art Immune Monitoring Discovery Platform. Thus, Post-Doctoral Researchers will have ample opportunities to develop their own projects and accelerate their careers to independency. To apply, please send a cover letter, CV and contact information for 3 references to Ephraim.Ansa-Addo@osumc.edu. Doctoral Degree Required Additional Information: The Ohio State University is a dynamic community of diverse resources, where opportunity thrives and where individuals transform themselves and the world. The Ohio State University is one of the nation’s largest and most comprehensive public universities and a top employer in Ohio. As one of only 50 designated comprehensive cancer centers in the nation, The Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center – Arthur G. James Cancer Hospital and Richard J. Solove Research Institute is dedicated to the creation of knowledge in laboratory, clinical and population-based cancer research. We apply those discoveries to develop more effective approaches to cancer prevention, diagnosis, and therapies – providing tomorrow’s standard of care today. A Cancer-Free World Begins Here. The OSUCCC – James is the only cancer program in the United States that features a National Cancer Institute (NCI)-designated comprehensive cancer center aligned with a nationally ranked academic medical center and a freestanding cancer hospital on the campus of one of the nation’s largest public universities. is the only cancer program in the United States that features a National Cancer Institute (NCI)-designated comprehensive cancer center aligned with a nationally ranked academic medical center and a freestanding cancer hospital on the campus of one of the nation’s largest public universities. Location: Pelotonia Research Center (1040) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/College-of-MedicineOffice-of-Health-Sciences/Post-Doctoral-Cardiovascular-Medicine_R158464-1": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral-Cardiovascular Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Post Doctoral-Cardiovascular Medicine Department: Medicine | IM Cardiovascular Medicine Post Doctoral Researcher to pursue specialized research training, education and experience under the guidance of a scientific mentor; plans, designs and executes experiments of considerable scope and complexity in the study of the role of cytoskeleton and signaling in the biogenesis and progression of heart disease and arrhythmia; collects and analyzes data for research sponsored by the National Institute of Health (NIH), as well as by other agencies; identifies and selects problems to be studied; develops and troubleshoots new experimental techniques and protocols; attends research seminars; contributes to manuscript preparation and supports technical writing; participates in preparation of grant applications for extramural funding.    Doctoral Degree in Biological Sciences Required Additional Information: Location: Davis Heart and Lung Research Institute (0113) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/OSUCareers/job/Columbus-Campus/Post-Doctoral-Researcher_R160962-1": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Post Doctoral Researcher Department: Veterinary Medicine | Veterinary Preventive Medicine The College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking applicants for a Post Doctoral Researcher. The Post Doctoral Researcher will be responsible for managing studies targeted at understanding infectious disease on the animal side of the human-animal interface. The Post Doctoral Researcher will be expected to conduct research, and provide technical assistance to the PI, students, and trainees as needed. The main roles for the individual hired for this position will include:  1) Manage multiple active surveillance projects in wild birds and exhibition swine to study various zoonotic diseases. This includes project planning and coordination; sample collection; sample testing; and data analysis.  2) Collaborating with the PI in the generation and testing of research hypotheses and data analysis, writing of papers, grants, and reports, and preparation of presentations and lectures. 3) Attending, participating, or presenting at laboratory meetings, seminars, graduate and undergraduate lectures, and conferences as needed. 4) Performing miscellaneous office duties as assigned by the PIs including, but not limited to, ordering supplies and helping the PIs in the organization and coordination of meetings and projects. 5) Maintaining frequent communication with other faculty and collaborators including students, veterinarians, producers, and livestock industry partners. Work hours will typically occur between normal business hours but may occasionally require early morning and late evening travel, and weekends.  This position is available for one year with the possibility of extension based on satisfactory performance and availability of funds.    Additional Information: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS AND EDUCATION PhD in veterinary medicine, animals science, or a related field      DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS AND EDUCATION: Experience working in a research laboratory  (PCR, ELISA)  Valid driver’s license  Prior field work experience (collection of biological samples from swine and wild birds  Previous experience with a lab information management system      WORKING CONDITIONS (List all physical working conditions required for the job)  Bench work   Field work at livestock shows, farms, and wildlife areas  Willingness to travel for sample collection      Location: Sisson Hall (0080) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
